Fix "Object of class ... could not be converted to string" in ForeignFieldQueryListener.

array_unique() defaults to SORT_STRING, which stringifies field objects while deduplicating.
Fields without __toString() (e.g. verbb\formie\fields\Name) throw during Form::find()->all().
SORT_REGULAR instead causes recursive object comparison ("Nesting level too deep") because
Craft fields reference their field layout. Replace the chain with an explicit loop that filters
to ForeignField and dedupes by uid, avoiding any object comparison.
Upstream: https://github.com/sebastian-lenz/craft-utils

--- a/src/foreignField/ForeignFieldQueryListener.php
+++ b/src/foreignField/ForeignFieldQueryListener.php
@@ -50,14 +50,14 @@
       ->getFields()
       ->getLayoutsByType($query->elementType);
 
-    $fields = array_filter(
-      array_unique(array_reduce(
-        $fieldLayouts,
-        fn($fields, $fieldLayout) => array_merge($fields, $fieldLayout->getCustomFields()),
-        []
-      )),
-      fn($field) => $field instanceof ForeignField
-    );
+    $fields = [];
+    foreach ($fieldLayouts as $fieldLayout) {
+      foreach ($fieldLayout->getCustomFields() as $field) {
+        if ($field instanceof ForeignField) {
+          $fields[$field->uid] = $field;
+        }
+      }
+    }
 
     foreach ($fields as $field) {
       $queryClass = $field::queryExtensionClass();
